you ready to order with the best deals?\" + \"Proceed to order\" button.\n11. **Footer**: dark bg; top cities grid (24 cities in 4 cols), Company/Contact/Legal columns, Follow Us social icons + newsletter field + Subscribe; divider; copyright.\n\nColors:\n- Primary orange #F17228, secondary yellow #FFB30E\n- Hero bg: gradient from #FFB30E (light tint) — original FoodWagon uses yellow gradient hero. Use linear gradient #FFB800 → #FF8A00-ish? Keep brand colors: gradient from #FFB30E to #F17228 for hero background, with white card overlay. Actually original design: hero bg is yellow gradient (#FFCE00-ish to orange). I'll do gradient #FFAE00 → #FF9500 using brand tones. Better: gradient from #FFB30E to #F17228 (both brand colors, satisfies requirement).\n- Text: #212121 dark, #616161 gray\n- Rating: #FFB30E star\n- Discount badge: yellow bg #FFB30E w/ white text; Fast badge: orange #F17228 bg white text\n- Open Now: green #79B93C bg tint; Opens tomorrow: orange tint\n- Footer: dark #212121\n\nType scale (Source Sans Pro):\n- H1 88 bold (hero \"Are you starving?\")\n- Section titles 43 bold\n- Card titles 22 bold\n- Body 18 regular\n- Buttons 18 bold\n\nLayout: 1920 wide, content max 1480 (padding 220) — original kit uses ~1480 container. Let's use 1480.\n\nFonts to load: \"Source Sans Pro\" — check availability. Family might be \"Source Sans Pro\" with styles \"Regular\", \"Bold\", \"SemiBold\" (for Source Sans Pro style naming: \"Regular\", \"Semibold\"?, actually Source Sans Pro styles: Regular, Italic, Bold, Semibold? Google Fonts: \"Source Sans Pro\" weights 200,300,400,600,700,900 → styles \"ExtraLight\",\"Light\",\"Regular\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\",\"Black\"). In Figma, font naming: family \"Source Sans Pro\", style \"SemiBold\" and \"Bold\". I'll try loading multiple and handle errors.\n\nSince these instances are components in the same file, `figma.createInstance()` requires the component to be accessible — components on other pages in same file work fine.\n\nRecoloring icons: create instance, find vector children, set fills. For instances, we can modify children of instance nodes (vector fills are overridable). Yes, instance child fill overrides allowed.\n\nImage fills: photos are components with image fills; instances can be resized; the fill may stretch. Component probably has fills on a rectangle/vector; resizing instance scales. To crop, we can resize instance and set scaleMode? Instance fill overrides: can set `fills` on instance if it's a single node? The photo symbols likely are vector/rectangle nodes with image fill. Resizing an instance keeps fill scale mode as is (probably FILL). Fine.\n\nPlan the build code. I'll write one big use_figma script but in manageable sections as instructed — multiple calls:\n\n1. Setup: load fonts, create main frame 01_Home, define helpers, create local components (maybe skip separate components page; brief says build reusable components in own file — we can create them on workspace page next to the frame).\n2. Header + Hero.\n3. Deals.\n4. How it works + Popular items.\n5. Featured restaurants.\n6. Search by food + Features.\n7. App promo + CTA + Footer.\n8. Screenshot & fix.\n\nActually for efficiency, I can build section-by-section with a persistent `cursor` y position — but separate tool calls don't share JS state. I'll instead pre-compute fixed Y offsets per section and set them in each call. Risk: if I need to adjust, frames are children of main frame with explicit positions; I can move later.\n\nLayout plan with fixed heights:\n- Header: y=0, h=112\n- Hero: y=112, h=620\n- Deals: y=732, h=3 cards * 360 + gaps... Deal cards: height 320 each, gap 80 → section h = 320*3+160+padding 120 = 1240. y=732 → ends 1972.\n\nHmm, let me simplify: give each section explicit y and height:\n\n- Header: 0–112 (112)\n- Hero: 112–752 (640)\n- Deals: 752–2032 (1280): pad 96 top, 3 cards h=340, gap 64 → 96+340*3+64*2+96 bottom? content 1480: 96+340+64+340+64+340 = 1244 +96 bottom=1340 → 752–2092\n- How it works: 2092–2672 (580): pad 80, title 54, gap 60, cards 280 → 80+54+60+280+106=580\n- Popular items: 2672–3256 (584): pad 80, title row 60, gap 48, cards 380, pad bottom 96? 80+60+48+384=572 +12... let's just 2672–3256.\n- Featured restaurants: 3256–4300 (1044): pad 80, title 54, gap 56, two rows of cards h=380, gap 40, view all button row 76+pad. 80+54+56+380+40+380+56+76 = 1122 → 3256–4378.\n- Search by Food: 4378–4978 (600): pad 80, title row 60, gap 56, circles 220 + label 30 → 80+60+56+220+24+36+80=556 → 4378–4934 (556)\n- Features: 4934–5414 (480): pad 80, cards 320 → 480.\n- App promo: 5414–5974 (560)\n- CTA: 5974–6474 (500)\n- Footer: 6474–7174 (700)\n\nTotal ~7174 height. OK.\n\nRather than rigidly precomputing, better approach: build main frame with vertical auto-layout! Then each section is a child with fixed height, and auto-layout stacks them. That avoids manual y math. Sections themselves use absolute positioning internally (no auto-layout) — simpler with many absolutely-placed items, though auto-layout inside helps too. Mixed approach: main frame vertical auto-layout, gap 0; each section frame fixed width 1920, height set; internal layout mostly absolute with a helper.\n\nActually auto-layout in main frame with children fixed heights: good.\n\nFor text, must load fonts first: I'll attempt \"Source Sans Pro\" styles: Regular, Bold, SemiBold, Italic? Load Regular+Bold+SemiBold. If load fails, fall back to \"Source Sans 3\"? Brief fixed font is Source Sans Pro. Try loading and catch errors.\n\nNote the Foundations text \"Aa Bb Cc...\" likely uses the font already, so it exists in file. Font family name might be \"Source Sans Pro\". Good.\n\nInstance creation: `figma.getNodeById('9:27')` returns component; `createInstance()` then `appendChild` to target — instances can be moved across pages, fine.\n\nLet me also check the components page Button (1:28) and Text Field (1:31) — brief says reuse the given default Button and Text Field as base. \"02 · Components gives only a default Button and a default Text Field... Design all other states... as reusable components in your file.\" So we should build our own component set (buttons variants etc.) in workspace. Reusing given components: use instances of 1:28/1:31 where default needed? They have specific sizes (200x60 button). Our buttons need different sizes. I'll create my own component set in the workspace (Buttons: primary/hover; TextField variants) referencing the given style (rounded corners etc.). Let me check the visual style of given button/textfield via screenshot to match. Let me screenshot components + a few media items quickly to understand appearance.\n\nLet me take screenshots: 1:24 (components frame) and 9:58 (media, big - maybe just part). Screenshot of 9:58 with maxDimension 1024 will be small; but useful to see photos style. Let me do 1:24 and 9:70 and 9:62 maybe. To save tokens, screenshot 1:24 and the whole media frame at low res.\n\nThen start building.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2939614a-de6b-46ec-9e1f-7271638640fe","uuid":"d8562644-2420-49b5-a33c-6f702824c5c2","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:15:00.974Z","thinking_duration_ms":46967}
