ntered (text x 72.5 in 200-wide button, centered). If I resize instance to 220 wide, does inner text stay centered? Text is at fixed position (x=72.5) inside the component, so resizing the instance scales positions?? For COMPONENT with no auto-layout, resizing the frame... The instance resize changes width; inner text constraints determine new position. The source button's text constraints — likely default left/top, so text would stay at x=72.5, not centered. Hmm.\n\nLet me check constraints of the button text. Actually, easier: build ALL buttons as my own local components (button w/ icon variants) using flat frames, and also use the given Text Field instance for the address input (that's the key reuse) plus a Button instance somewhere with default size (200x60, \"Proceed to order\" style or Order Now). I'll use instances of the source Button where label fits centered: e.g., \"Order Now\" buttons (5x), \"View All\", \"Subscribe\", \"Proceed to order\". For those I keep default 200x60 or resize carefully.\n\nCheck constraints first: query the text node inside 1:28 for constraints. Let me just query quickly and then decide. Also verify whether instance text x can be overridden — no (relative-transform can't be overridden on instance children).\n\nPlan: rebuild hero:\n- tfInst placeholder stays at x=20 — the marker icon overlapping text \"Enter Your Address\"? Placeholder text starts at x=20 within field; icon at field x+16 would overlap text. Alternative: put marker icon to the right side of the field? Or above? In original FoodWagon, icon is left of placeholder. Since I can't move the placeholder text inside instance... Can I override characters only. Hmm — workaround: detach instance? The brief says reuse; detached instance loses component link but keeps visual. Better approach: set placeholder text with leading spaces? Hacky but text auto-size... Placeholder \"Enter Your Address\" with 3 leading spaces shifts right. Width auto-adjusts. Leading spaces render. That keeps instance reuse. Slightly hacky but fine visually. Actually spaces width ~4px at 16px font ≈ 12px — need ~28px shift → 6 spaces. Ugh, imprecise but ok. Alternative: place marker icon at right edge of the field (like a trailing icon) — looks intentional and clean. I'll do trailing marker icon at field right edge. Hmm, but spec: address field \"Enter Your Address\" (Icon_Map_Marker) — icon included somewhere in field. Trailing icon is a legit design decision. Do that.\n\n- Find Food button: use Button instance resized? Label centering issue. Instead build flat button frame (rect + icon + text), name it \"Button / Find Food\". Fine.\n\nAlso for the overlay wash: rect inserted before heroCon; secHero children order: heroBg, overlay, heroCon? heroCon was already child (first). After cleanup secHero only had heroCon. I appended heroBg (after heroCon) and overlay (after heroBg), then secHero.appendChild(heroCon) moves heroCon to top. Good.\n\nCleanup: heroCon now has children (texts, card, tabs, tfInst...). Error occurred at ph.x — so everything up to marker icon inst exists: headline, subtext, card, tabs, divider, tfInst, marker icon. The tfInst is fine. I'll clean heroCon children again and rebuild fully with fixes.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2939614a-de6b-46ec-9e1f-7271638640fe","uuid":"7d83868b-5e1c-4867-ad18-d5109b574da3","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:23:18.288Z","thinking_duration_ms":25200}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":39080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"081d6ae7e5e30a7a50da6c3357e2ab52","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Instance child positions can't be overridden — rebuilding hero with flat buttons and a trailing icon in the field."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2939614a-de6b-46ec-9e1f-7271638640fe","uuid":"9bdf15c0-a2e9-4eaa-a7fc-5aaf337fd27e","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:23:19.140Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":39080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"081d6ae7e5e30a7a50da6c3357e2ab52","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_23_c2d74be3","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Source Sans Pro', style:'Regular'});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Source Sans Pro', style:'Bold'});\nfunction inst(id, x, y, parent, w) {\n  const c = figma.getNodeById(id);\n  const i = c.createInstance();\n  parent.appendChild(i);\n  i.x = x; i.y = y;\n  if (w && i.width !== w) i.resize(w, i.height * w / i.width);\n  return i;\n}\nfunction instCover(id, x, y, w, h, parent) {\n  const c = figma.getNodeById(id);\n  const i = c.createInstance();\n  parent.appendChild(i);\n  const fills = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(i.fills));\n  if (fills.length && fills[0].type==='IMAGE') { fills[0].scaleMode='FILL'; i.fills=fills; }\n  i.resize(w, h);\n  i.x = x; i.y = y;\n  return i;\n}\nfunction text(parent, str, fontSize, style, color, x, y) {\n  const t = figma.createText();\n  t.fontName = {family:'Source Sans Pro', style};\n  t.fontSize = fontSize;\n  t.characters = str;\n  t.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color}];\n  t.x = x; t.y = y;\n  parent.appendChild(t);\n  return t;\n}\nfunction rect(parent, x, y, w, h, fill, radius) {\n  const r = figma.createRectangle();\n  r.x = x; r.y = y; r.resize(w, h);\n  r.fills = fill ? [{type:'SOLID', color: fill}] : [];\n  if (radius) r.cornerRadius = radius;\n  parent.appendChild(r);\n  return r;\n}\nfunction iconBtn(parent, name, x, y, w, h, label, iconId, fill, labelColor, iconColor, radius) {\n  const f = figma.createFrame();\n  f.name = name;\n  f.resize(w, h); f.x = x; f.y = y;\n  f.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color: fill}];\n  f.cornerRadius = radius != null ? radius : 10;\n  parent.appendChild(f);\n  const t = text(f, label, 18, 'Bold', labelColor, 0, 0);\n  const labelW = t.width;\n  const iconW = 24, gap = 10;\n  const total = iconId ? iconW + gap + labelW : labelW;\n  const startX = (w - total) / 2;\n  let cx = startX;\n  if (iconId) {\n    const ic = inst(iconId, cx, (h-24)/2, f, 24);\n    for (const v of ic.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR')) v.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:iconColor}];\n    cx += iconW + gap;\n  }\n  t.x = cx; t.y = (h - t.height)/2;\n  return f;\n}\nconst ORANGE={r:0.94509804,g:0.44705883,b:0.15686275}, YELLOW={r:1,g:0.70196078,b:0.05490196},\n  INK={r:0.14509804,g:0.15294118,b:0.16862745}, GRAY={r:0.39215686,g:0.39607843,b:0.42352941},\n  LIGHT={r:0.61960784,g:0.61960784,b:0.65098039}, WHITE={r:1,g:1,b:1};\n\nconst secHero = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('13:4');\nconst heroCon = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('13:16');\nfor (const ch of [...heroCon.children]) ch.remove();\nfor (const ch of [...secHero.children]) if (ch.id !== heroCon.id) ch.remove();\n\nconst heroBg = instCover('9:55', 0, 0, 1920, 720, secHero);\nconst overlay = rect(secHero, 0, 0, 1150, 720, YELLOW, 0);\noverlay.opacity = 0.85;\nsecHero.appendChild(heroCon);\n\ntext(heroCon, 'Are you starving?', 68, 'Bold', INK, 0, 0);\ntext(heroCon, 'Within a few clicks, find meals that are accessible near you', 26, 'Regular', GRAY, 0, 96);\n\nconst card = figma.createFrame();\ncard.name='Hero Search Card';\ncard.resize(880, 300); card.x=0; card.y=176;\ncard.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:WHITE}];\ncard.cornerRadius=16;\ncard.effects=[{type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.5,g:0.3,b:0.05,a:0.15},offset:{x:0,y:24},radius:48,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'}];\nheroCon.appendChild(card);\n\nconst tabDel = figma.createFrame();\ntabDel.name='Tab · Delivery (current)';\ntabDel.resize(180,64); tabDel.x=24; tabDel.y=24;\ntabDel.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:YELLOW}]; tabDel.cornerRadius=10;\ncard.appendChild(tabDel);\ninst('9:10', 20, 20, tabDel, 24);\ntext(tabDel,'Delivery',18,'Bold',INK,54,20);\n\nconst tabPick = figma.createFrame();\ntabPick.name='Tab · Pickup';\ntabPick.resize(160,64); tabPick.x=216; tabPick.y=24;\ntabPick.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:{r:0.955,g:0.955,b:0.96}}]; tabPick.cornerRadius=10;\ncard.appendChild(tabPick);\ninst('9:13', 20, 20, tabPick, 24);\ntext(tabPick,'Pickup',18,'Bold',GRAY,54,20);\n\nrect(card, 24, 104, 832, 1, {r:0.93,g:0.93,b:0.93}, 0);\n\nconst tfInst = figma.getNodeById('1:31').createInstance();\ncard.appendChild(tfInst);\ntfInst.x=24; tfInst.y=128;\ntfInst.resize(560, tfInst.height);\ntfInst.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT'&&n.name==='Label').characters='Address';\ntfInst.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT'&&n.name==='Placeholder').characters='Enter Your Address';\n// trailing marker icon inside the input (right edge)\ninst('9:9', 24+560-20-24, 128+26+16, card, 24);\n\nconst ffb = iconBtn(card, 'Button · Find Food', 636, 154, 220, 64, 'Find Food', '9:12', ORANGE, WHITE, WHITE, 10);\nffb.effects=[{type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.94509804,g:0.44705883,b:0.15686275,a:0.35},offset:{x:0,y:10},radius:20,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'}];\n\nconst noodles = inst('9:39', 1180, 60, heroCon, 480);\nnoodles.effects=[{type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.4,g:0.25,b:0.02,a:0.35},offset:{x:-16,y:40},radius:64,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'}];\nreturn 'hero ok';\n","description":"Rebuild Hero with flat Find Food button and trailing map-marker icon in address field","fileKey":"vxs2YHWWLo4u0YPXrkb2yt"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2939614a-de6b-46ec-9e1f-7271638640fe","uuid":"82a2632c-9272-42f8-adda-251fab003134","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:23:41.135Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_23_c2d74be3","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
